    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "THE MATH",
      "new_visual_element": "The chain rule, and what happens where paths meet",
      "narration": "The entire engine is one rule, applied over and over. If the loss depends on y, and y depends on x, then how much the loss moves when you nudge x is how much it moves with y, multiplied by how much y moves with x. You multiply the local derivatives along the path. And where several paths reach the same value, you add them together.",
      "narration_text": "The entire engine is one rule, applied over and over. If the loss depends on y, and y depends on x, then how much the loss moves when you nudge x is how much it moves with y, multiplied by how much y moves with x. You multiply the local derivatives along the path. And where several paths reach the same value, you add them together.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "TypesetMath",
          "props": {
            "title": "One rule, applied in reverse",
            "rows": [
