      "new_visual_element": "The gradient igniting at the loss and burning backwards (my own Manim scene)",
      "narration": "This is that rule running on the real graph from my repo. The forward pass flows left to right. Then the gradient ignites at the loss and burns backward through the tape, composing each local derivative as it goes. One detail I left in on purpose: the input node never lights up, because inputs do not require gradients, and the engine really does stop the burn there.",
